    body: '- Net profit = total revenue - total cost\n- Gross margin = total revenue - variable cost\n- Break-even output = fixed cost / (price - variable cost per unit)\n- Straight-line depreciation = (cost - salvage value) / useful life\n- Opportunity cost = value of the next best alternative given up\n- Price elasticity of demand = percentage change in quantity demanded / percentage change in price\n- Field area in hectares = length (m) x width (m) / 10,000\n- Cow gestation about 283 days; sow 114 days; ewe and doe about 150 days; mare about 340 days\n- Chicken egg incubation 21 days; day-old chicks are separated by vent sexing\n- Daily dry matter intake for cattle about 2 to 3 per cent of body weight\n- Thermometer for temperature, barometer for pressure, hygrometer for humidity, anemometer for wind speed, rain gauge for rainfall in mm\n- Sand 0.05 to 2 mm, silt 0.002 to 0.05 mm, clay below 0.002 mm; loam holds roughly equal parts\n- Field capacity is water held after drainage; permanent wilting point is where roots can extract no more\n- Drip irrigation puts over 90 per cent of applied water to the crop, flood irrigation only about 40 to 70 per cent\n- Grain dried to 10 to 14 per cent moisture stores safely\n- Pasteurisation: 63 degrees Celsius for 30 minutes, or 72 degrees Celsius for 15 seconds\n- Annual rainfall falls from over 2,000 mm on the coast to about 500 mm in the extreme north\n- Harmattan blows from the Sahara from December to February; monsoon air comes inland from the Atlantic'
